msgid "spyder_ruby_plaque"
msgstr ""
"Ruby is just the term for any corundum that is red! \n"
"\n"
" When corundum comes in other colors like blue, pink and clear, it is called "
"a sapphire. \n"
"\n"
" When tuxemon eat rubies, they become passionate and vigorous, making them "
"better at physical attacks like slaps, claws and bites."

msgid "spyder_opal_plaque"
msgstr ""
"Opals show flashes of colored light. \n"
"\n"
" They form in fissues and dips in rock when water evaporates leaving behind "
"silica. \n"
"\n"
" Tuxemon that eat opals benefit from its magical warding are better able to "
"escape magical distant attacks like blasts, sprays and rays."

msgid "spyder_emerald_plaque"
msgstr ""
"An emerald is a green variety of beryl. Beryl that is blue is called "
"aquamarine instead. \n"
"\n"
" A one-carat emerald is larger but less dense than a one-carat diamond. \n"
"\n"
" Tuxemon that eat emeralds have their sight and intuition heighten, making "
"their ranged attacks like shots, sprays and blasts more potent."

msgid "spyder_agate_plaque"
msgstr ""
"Agate is a rock, often formed by volcanoes and often banded with parallel "
"lines. \n"
"\n"
" It features a great variety of colors: browns, grays, creams, reds, oranges "
"and even blues. \n"
"\n"
" Feeding agate to a tuxemon can increase its speed and agility, making it "
"faster to react in battle."

msgid "spyder_diamond_plaque"
msgstr ""
"Famously the hardest gemstone in the world, diamonds are great on necklaces, "
"engagement rings and earrings! \n"
"\n"
" If your fiance doesn't buy a Shaft diamond ring for you, he doesn't love "
"you! \n"
"\n"
" Feed diamonds to your tuxemon to harden their skin, making them better able "
"to resist physical blows."

msgid "spyder_quartz_plaque"
msgstr ""
"Quartz is one of the most abundant minerals on the planet. \n"
"\n"
" Some quartz varieties - like onyx, amethyst and carnelian - are rarer and "
"more precious. \n"
"\n"
" Quartz is used in clocks to keep very precise time. \n"
"\n"
" Tuxemon that eat quartz have their fortitude and vitality increased, making "
"them able to endure more attacks before being knocked out. "

msgid "spyder_shaft_plaque"
msgstr "Sponsored by Shaft. \"We dig it!\""

msgid "spyder_nimrod_plaque"
msgstr "Sponsored by Nimrod. \"If we didn't sell them, someone else would!\""

msgid "spyder_nimrod2_plaque"
msgstr ""
"Tuxemon are powerful weapons that have fought alongside humans for as long "
"as there has been war. \n"
"\n"
" Rock paintings found in caves show prehistoric humans training saber-"
"toothed Rockats to fight wild Wolffsky."

msgid "spyder_nimrod3_plaque"
msgstr ""
"The symbol of an ancient empire was the Eaglace, because when the empire "
"invaded from the icy north their generals and scouts rode on Eaglace. \n"
"\n"
" Today, medic teams in our mighty republic are training with Agnidon for "
"protection and transport. "

msgid "spyder_nimrod4_plaque"
msgstr ""
"But soon, tuxemon and humans may be rendered obsolete. \n"
"\n"
" Our corporate sponsors Nimrod are developing robot technology that could "
"make war a bloodless affair. \n"
"\n"
" In the meantime, sign up for the Nimrod Enforcers for good pay, free "
"education and a life of adventure."

msgid "spyder_nimrod5_plaque"
msgstr ""
"At Nimrod, we believe that technology has the power to transform the world "
"for the better.\n"
"\n"
" Our unwavering commitment to innovation drives us to develop groundbreaking "
"solutions that address the challenges of today and tomorrow.\n"
"\n"
" From advancing healthcare to protecting our planet, Nimrod is dedicated to "
"creating a brighter future for all."

msgid "spyder_shaft1_sign"
msgstr "Shaft Headquarters: Mining Division"

msgid "spyder_shaft2_sign"
msgstr "Shaft Headquarters: Public Relations Division"

msgid "spyder_leather_note1"
msgstr ""
"*rummages through the trash can, pulling out a banana peel with a few days' "
"worth of mold on it* Ugh, wait, what's this? A leather notebook...\n"
"\n"
" Letter from Dr Henry, Former Nimrod Researcher\n"
"\n"
" I used to work for Nimrod, but I quit due to their priorities. They care "
"more about profit and power than the well-being of tuxemon and their "
"handlers.\n"
"\n"
" I've seen firsthand the devastating effects of Nimrod's tuxemon breeding "
"programs.\n"
"\n"
" They're pushing these creatures to their limits, and it's only a matter of "
"time before something goes terribly wrong."

msgid "spyder_leather_note2"
msgstr ""
"*digs deeper into the trash can, pushing aside banana peels and broken pens* "
"Gross. Okay, what's this? Another notebook...\n"
"\n"
" Field Notes of Dr Sophia, Conservation Biologist\n"
"\n"
" My team and I have been monitoring tuxemon populations in the wild, and our "
"data suggests that their numbers are declining at an alarming rate.\n"
"\n"
" This is likely due to habitat destruction and fragmentation, as well as the "
"increasing demand for tuxemon for military and commercial purposes.\n"
"\n"
" We've observed that tuxemon are playing a crucial role in maintaining "
"ecosystem balance in certain regions.\n"
"\n"
" Their loss could have far-reaching consequences for the environment and "
"human societies that depend on these ecosystems."

msgid "spyder_leather_note3"
msgstr ""
"*pulls out a moldy pizza box and a stack of old newspapers* This trash can "
"is a treasure trove of grossness. Oh, a journal...\n"
"\n"
" Journal of Dr John, Historian\n"
"\n"
" My research on the ancient empire's use of tuxemon has led me to question "
"the official narrative.\n"
"\n"
" It appears that the empire's relationship with tuxemon was more complex and "
"nuanced than previously thought...\n"
"\n"
" with evidence of both reverence and exploitation.\n"
"\n"
" I've discovered a series of ancient texts that suggest the empire's use of "
"tuxemon was not solely for military purposes...\n"
"\n"
" but also for spiritual and ceremonial reasons.\n"
"\n"
" These texts, written in a long-forgotten language, offer a glimpse into a "
"world where tuxemon were revered as sacred beings.\n"
"\n"
" As I delve deeper, I'm uncovering a rich tapestry of stories and legends... "
"revealing the empire's profound connection to the tuxemon.\n"
"\n"
" Fascinating and unsettling, it raises more questions than answers about the "
"empire's rulers."

msgid "spyder_leather_note4"
msgstr ""
"*reaches to the bottom of the trash can, pulling out a soggy notebook* Ugh, "
"I hope this one isn't ruined. Ah, it's still legible...\n"
"\n"
" Notebook of Dr Maria, Tuxemon Biologist\n"
"\n"
" Observations of tuxemon behavior in the wild suggest that they are highly "
"social creatures...\n"
"\n"
" with complex communication patterns and a strong sense of hierarchy.\n"
"\n"
" This challenges the common assumption that tuxemon are simply tools for "
"human use.\n"
"\n"
" Preliminary data suggests that tuxemon are capable of experiencing stress "
"and anxiety when subjected to intense training regimens.\n"
"\n"
" Further research is needed to understand the long-term effects of this "
"stress on tuxemon well-being."

msgid "spyder_leather_sarah_greeting"
msgstr ""
"Hey, what's up? I've been worried about my girlfriend lately. She's been "
"acting really strange.\n"
"\n"
" Do you want to know what's been going on with her?"

msgid "spyder_leather_sarah_yes"
msgstr "Okay, I'll tell you. I was there..."

msgid "spyder_leather_sarah_no"
msgstr "No problem. I just thought you should know."

msgid "spyder_leather_sarah_after"
msgstr "I'm worried. What if we can't fix this? What if it's too late?"

msgid "spyder_leather_sarah1"
msgstr ""
"I don't know, Sarah. I'm feeling really conflicted about the mine right now. "
"We've been getting some...\n"
"\n"
" unusual requests from our investors. Changes in our priorities."

msgid "spyder_leather_sarah2"
msgstr ""
"What's going on? You've been distant lately. Is everything okay? What kind \n"
"of requests?"

msgid "spyder_leather_sarah3"
msgstr ""
"I'm not supposed to say. But let's just say that our investors are very "
"interested in the history of this place.\n"
"\n"
" I think they're looking for something specific. Something that could change "
"everything."

msgid "spyder_leather_sarah4"
msgstr ""
"But what about the mine? What about the people who work here? You didn't \n"
"know what would happen. You didn't know about the eggs."

msgid "spyder_leather_sarah5"
msgstr ""
"That's no excuse. I should have known better. I should have thought about "
"the consequences.\n"
"\n"
" I'm one of the ones who proposed diverting the river and draining the lake. "
"I'm one of the ones who made this happen."

msgid "spyder_leather_sarah6"
msgstr ""
"You're doing the right thing now. You're trying to make it right. I'm here \n"
"for you. We'll get through this together."

msgid "spyder_leather_sarah7"
msgstr ""
"I hope so. I really do. But it's hard to shake off the feeling of guilt. \n"
"It's hard to forget what we've done."

